  "seminaryName": "Notre Dame Seminary",
  "voice": {
    "weather": [
      "Summer is a wet heat that starts in May and does not lift until All Saints, and the church is the only cold room in the parish.",
      "Hurricane season is a category of weather and a category of prayer; the pastor watches the cone on his phone during the collection.",
      "The one cold week in January catches the whole city without coats, and the eight o'clock Mass is a row of blankets.",
      "Carnival is weather too: three weeks in which nothing can be scheduled and the parades decide which streets a funeral can use."
    ],
    "sunday": [
      "The Uptown Masses are seersucker and a second line to brunch; the Seventh Ward Masses are a gospel choir and a homily that will take the time it takes.",
      "The Vietnamese Mass in the East fills the church and the lot and a second building, and the collection is counted by a committee.",
      "On the North Shore the parking lots are full of trucks and the pastor greets each family by the name of their grandmother's parish in the city."
    ],
    "presbyterate": [
      "The priests of New Orleans cook, and a deanery meeting is a pot of something on a stove and an argument about the roux.",
      "They know which archbishop ordained every man in the room and hold it against him, gently, forever.",
      "Half of them were somewhere else for a year after the storm and speak of it the way soldiers speak of a war."
    ]
  },
